    "summary": {
      "candidates": [
        {
          "evidence": [
            {
              "locator": "metadata",
              "original_text": "{\"id\": \"Q4689062\", \"labels\": {\"en\": \"Afghan Defense University\"}, \"descriptions\": {}}",
              "source_ref": "s1"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:lead",
              "original_text": "Marshal Fahim National Defense University (MFNDU) is a military university located in Kabul, the capital city of Afghanistan.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Geography",
              "original_text": "The university's campus in Qargha is spread over an area of 400 acres. The campus includes academic and administrative buildings, student dormitories, faculty housing, sports facilities, and a library.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Geography",
              "original_text": "lying on the western outskirts of Kabul",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:lead",
              "original_text": "MFNDU educates and trains military officers, senior civil servants, and professionals from various government and non-government organizations in Afghanistan and other partner nations.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Islamic_Republic_period",
              "original_text": "American contractors moved in mid-2008 to clear the site, which previously served a variety of military roles since the Soviet–Afghan War.[4]",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Islamic_Republic_period",
              "original_text": "A cornerstone-laying ceremony was conducted in April 2010 and the construction was completed in 2013.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:National_Military_Academy",
              "original_text": "NMAA moved to the ANDU site in Qargha upon completion of its new campus in 2012. It was previously located in the old Air Academy established by the Soviet Union to the north of Kabul beside Kabul International Airport.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Islamic_Republic_period",
              "original_text": "In April 2014, the university was renamed the Defense University of Marshal Fahim in honour of the former Vice President of Afghanistan, Mohammed Fahim who died of a heart attack on 9 March 2014.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:lead",
              "original_text": "MFNDU provides undergraduate, graduate, and postgraduate programs in various fields, including military science, defense studies, strategic studies, leadership and management, international relations, law, and engineering. The university also offers short-term courses, workshops, and seminars for professionals in specific fields, conducts research on various security and defense-related issues, and publishes academic papers, reports, and policy briefs.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:National_Military_Academy",
              "original_text": "NMAA cadets study both military and academic subjects for a total of 4 years and are awarded a degree from ANDU before commissioning into the ANA as Second Lieutenants.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            },
            {
              "locator": "section:Afghan_National_Army_Officer_Academy_.28ANAOA.29",
              "original_text": "The ANA Officer Academy accepted its first intake of 270 students selected from approximately 10,000 initial applicants in October 2013.",
              "source_ref": "s2"
            }
          ],
          "id": "c1",
          "value": {
            "language": "en",
            "text": "Marshal Fahim National Defense University, also known as Afghan Defense University, is a military university in Kabul, Afghanistan. Its campus at Qargha, on the western outskirts of the city, includes teaching and administrative buildings, student accommodation, faculty housing, sports facilities and a library. The institution trains military officers, senior civil servants and professionals from government and non-government organizations in Afghanistan and partner nations.\n\nThe Qargha site was prepared for the planned university from mid-2008. A cornerstone-laying ceremony followed in April 2010, and construction was completed in 2013. The National Military Academy of Afghanistan had moved to the site in 2012 from its earlier location beside Kabul International Airport. In April 2014, the university was renamed in honour of former Vice President Mohammed Fahim.\n\nIts academic provision encompasses undergraduate, graduate and postgraduate programs, with fields including military science, defense and strategic studies, leadership and management, international relations, law and engineering. Short courses and professional seminars complement these programs. National Military Academy cadets undertake four years of military and academic study and receive an ANDU degree before commissioning. The separate ANA Officer Academy accepted an initial cohort of 270 students in October 2013; that figure describes academy intake rather than total university enrolment."
          },
          "verification": "supported"
        }
      ],
